ticity), Remap (Measure OffsetX/OffsetY/Distance/Direction/TargetAngle/TargetScale/TargetOpacity, FromRange -> Drive OffsetX/OffsetY/Angle/Scale/ScaleX/ScaleY/Opacity over ToRange, bClamp, curve), Pointer Parallax (Depth, Tilt, Area Screen or AreaWidget).
 
 ## Constraint recipes
-Ball round a ring: Follow Path, ShapeOutline of an Ellipse, Speed 0.25. Eyes following the cursor: on each pupil Copy Position -> Pointer, CopyAmount 0.15, bSmooth, WhileAnimated FollowKeys; then Stay Inside the eye white (Ellipse) - keyed looks on the pupil's Transform track then spring there inside the eye. Magnetic button: Copy Position -> Pointer, CopyAmount 0.3, Activation NearPointer, bLimit +-12, bSmooth Bounce 0.3. Dial knob: Follow Path Circle, ClosestToTarget -> Pointer (HoldLast), Activation WhilePressed. Trail: each dot Copy Position -> the previous dot, bSmooth. Dock magnify: Remap Distance (from edges) 0..150 -> Scale 1.5..1 toward the Pointer. Blueprint: Get Widget Constraints(widget), Find Constraint (by Name, or the kind's name e.g. "Follow Path"), Get Constraint Names, Add Constraint(class), Set Constraint Value(name, channel Strength/PathPosition/OffsetX/OffsetY/AngleOffset/Distance), Set Constraint Value By Name(name, value name, value) - any number or switch as the Details name it: "Path Position", "Strength", "Distance", "Copy Amount X", "Offset Y", "Radius X", "Target Point Y", "Orient" -, Set Target Widget, Reset Constraint Motion. Widget Animation track "Constraint" (category Interaction): ConstraintName (None = first), ValueName (any number by that name; None = the old Channel), Start/End Value; a new one on a Follow Path starts on Path Position, one lap. To key a PLACE (where eyes look, where something aims), don't key numbers: add a Constraint Target widget (UWidgetConstraintTarget, invisible, MarkerSize, crosshair in the designer), point the constraints' Target (Kind Widget) at it and key its Transform track - 2D keys, motion path, gizmo. Eyes looking where keyed: each pupil Copy Position -> Widget LookTarget (CopyAmount 1) then Stay Inside its eye (Ellipse); key LookTarget's Transform; give LookTarget Copy Position -> Pointer with WhileAnimated LetGo to follow the cursor between keyed glances.
